# GitLab Pages reads this file; GitHub Pages has no equivalent and ignores it. Kept so the
# intent is recorded and so the site still behaves if it is ever served from somewhere
# that honours it -- Netlify and Cloudflare Pages use the same format.
#
# On GitHub Pages the two rules below degrade rather than break:
#   /sr-lat/*  404s instead of redirecting. Nothing links there; it was a duplicate of the
#              bare Latin URL whose canonical already pointed away from it.
#   /*/ulica/* is served 404.html, which boots the app and routes itself, so the page is
#              correct but the status line says 404. Street pages are not in the sitemap
#              and are reached from the site's own search, so nothing depends on the code.

# Latin is the canonical form and is served bare, so /sr-lat is the same page twice.
/sr-lat/* /:splat

# Street pages are not prerendered -- 58,947 streets across three locales would be a
# hundred and seventy thousand files for URLs nobody reaches from outside the site.
/*/ulica/* /404.html 200
